{"id":"d8b71b9d0560051f695b7cb1639cf26582249571","axis":"silent","repo":"falcosecurity/falco","sha":"d8b71b9d0560051f695b7cb1639cf26582249571","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/workflows/image-trust.yaml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@","+name: Image trust","+","+on:","+  pull_request:","+    branches:","+      - master","+      - release/*","+    paths:","+      - docker/**","+      - test/container-trust/**","+      - .github/workflows/image-trust.yaml","+      - .github/workflows/reusable_build_docker.yaml","+  workflow_dispatch:","+","+permissions:","+  contents: read","+","+concurrency:","+  group: image-trust-${{ github.ref }}","+  cancel-in-progress: true","+","+jobs:","+  build-and-test-images:","+    strategy:","+      fail-fast: false","+      matrix:","+        arch: [x86_64, aarch64]","+    uses: ./.github/workflows/reusable_build_docker.yaml","+    with:","+      arch: ${{ matrix.arch }}","+      # Exercise image construction using an already published package. The","+      # package CI separately builds and tests the components pinned by this PR.","+      # Master and release workflows test these images with their new packages.","+      version: '0.45.1'","+      tag: trust-${{ github.run_id }}"],"additions":35,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":".github/workflows/reusable_build_docker.yaml","lines":["@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ jobs:"," ","       - name: Build falco image","         run: |","-          docker build -f docker/falco/Dockerfile -t docker.io/falcosecurity/falco:${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }} \\","+          docker build --pull --no-cache -f docker/falco/Dockerfile -t docker.io/falcosecurity/falco:${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }} \\","             --build-arg VERSION_BUCKET=bin${{ inputs.bucket_suffix }} \\","             --build-arg FALCO_VERSION=${{ inputs.version }} \\","             --build-arg FALCO_COMMIT_SHA=${{ github.sha }} \\","@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ jobs:"," ","       - name: Build falco-debian image","         run: |","-          docker build -f docker/falco-debian/Dockerfile -t docker.io/falcosecurity/falco:${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }}-debian \\","+          docker build --pull --no-cache -f docker/falco-debian/Dockerfile -t docker.io/falcosecurity/falco:${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }}-debian \\","             --build-arg VERSION_BUCKET=deb${{ inputs.bucket_suffix }} \\","             --build-arg FALCO_VERSION=${{ inputs.version }} \\","             --build-arg FALCO_COMMIT_SHA=${{ github.sha }} \\","@@ -62,8 +62,9 @@ jobs:","             docker save docker.io/falcosecurity/falco:${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }}-debian --output /tmp/falco-${{ inputs.arch }}-debian.tar"," ","       - name: Build falco-driver-loader image","+        # Use the Debian image built above; it has not been published yet.","         run: |","-          docker build -f docker/driver-loader/Dockerfile -t docker.io/falcosecurity/falco-driver-loader:${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }} \\","+          docker build --no-cache -f docker/driver-loader/Dockerfile -t docker.io/falcosecurity/falco-driver-loader:${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }} \\","             --build-arg FALCO_IMAGE_TAG=${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }} \\","             --build-arg FALCO_VERSION=${{ inputs.version }} \\","             --build-arg FALCO_COMMIT_SHA=${{ github.sha }} \\","@@ -73,7 +74,7 @@ jobs:"," ","       - name: Build falco-driver-loader-buster image","         run: |","-          docker build -f docker/driver-loader-buster/Dockerfile -t docker.io/falcosecurity/falco-driver-loader:${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }}-buster \\","+          docker build --pull --no-cache -f docker/driver-loader-buster/Dockerfile -t docker.io/falcosecurity/falco-driver-loader:${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }}-buster \\","             --build-arg VERSION_BUCKET=deb${{ inputs.bucket_suffix }} \\","             --build-arg FALCO_VERSION=${{ inputs.version }} \\","             --build-arg FALCO_COMMIT_SHA=${{ github.sha }} \\","@@ -81,6 +82,28 @@ jobs:","             .","             docker save docker.io/falcosecurity/falco-driver-loader:${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }}-buster --output /tmp/falco-driver-loader-${{ inputs.arch }}-buster.tar"," ","+      - name: Verify image certificate trust","+        env:","+          IMAGE_TAG: ${{ inputs.arch }}-${{ inputs.tag }}","+        run: |","+          for image in \\","+            \"docker.io/falcosecurity/falco:${IMAGE_TAG}\" \\","+            \"docker.io/falcosecurity/falco:${IMAGE_TAG}-debian\" \\","+            \"docker.io/falcosecurity/falco-driver-loader:${IMAGE_TAG}\" \\","+            \"docker.io/falcosecurity/falco-driver-loader:${IMAGE_TAG}-buster\"; do","+            echo \"Checking ${image}\"","+            docker run --rm --network none --entrypoint /bin/sh \\","+              --mount \"type=bind,src=${GITHUB_WORKSPACE}/test/container-trust,dst=/test-trust,readonly\" \\","+              \"${image}\" -ec '","+                sh /test-trust/check-trust.sh","+                update-ca-certificates --fresh","+                sh /test-trust/check-trust.sh","+              '","+            docker run --rm --entrypoint curl \"${image}\" \\","+              --fail --silent --show-error --location --max-time 60 \\","+              --output /dev/null https://download.falco.org/","+          done","+","       - name: Upload images tarballs","         uses: actions/upload-artifact@65c4c4a1ddee5b72f698fdd19549f0f0fb45cf08 # v4.6.0","         with:"],"additions":27,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"CMakeLists.txt","lines":["@@ -294,11 +294,11 @@ if(NOT WIN32","    AND NOT MUSL_OPTIMIZED_BUILD"," )"," \tinclude(falcoctl)","-\tset(CONTAINER_VERSION \"0.7.5\")","+\tset(CONTAINER_VERSION \"0.7.6\")"," \tif(${CMAKE_HOST_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} STREQUAL \"x86_64\")","-\t\tset(CONTAINER_HASH \"ac29cbb16aa3c9bbb290e6533aef9a9a39943ffa1be6e1a2ed8ff1c3780b5d9b\")","+\t\tset(CONTAINER_HASH \"44d61eff009ed9b693ad065b07738d5b90cc264fe195d3d11a24e94e60e17bb1\")"," \telse() # arm64","-\t\tset(CONTAINER_HASH \"907a54f1bdbad59cbc137859c66be1f315c3556ecf42b012592fb6b5818b0374\")","+\t\tset(CONTAINER_HASH \"3971b047c95d656eb4dd420385ba7a7035f0b3c3d874301dca66a241403c92e7\")"," \tendif()"," \tinclude(container_plugin)"," "],"additions":3,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"cmake/modules/falcoctl.cmake","lines":["@@ -20,16 +20,16 @@ option(ADD_FALCOCTL_DEPENDENCY \"Add falcoctl dependency while building falco\" ON"," if(ADD_FALCOCTL_DEPENDENCY)"," \tstring(TOLOWER ${CMAKE_HOST_SYSTEM_NAME} FALCOCTL_SYSTEM_NAME)"," ","-\tset(FALCOCTL_VERSION \"0.14.2\")","+\tset(FALCOCTL_VERSION \"0.14.3\")"," "," \tmessage(STATUS \"Building with falcoctl: ${FALCOCTL_VERSION}\")"," "," \tif(${CMAKE_HOST_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR} STREQUAL \"x86_64\")"," \t\tset(FALCOCTL_SYSTEM_PROC_GO \"amd64\")","-\t\tset(FALCOCTL_HASH \"9e0c12abdee6f042cffaf33b8bc4103e70f68a597f4d02310e2aa06a860310df\")","+\t\tset(FALCOCTL_HASH \"263a6c773b4d24af1e6827ea2f63ac7c50678becf58e607390eb8976dee08af1\")"," \telse() # aarch64"," \t\tset(FALCOCTL_SYSTEM_PROC_GO \"arm64\")","-\t\tset(FALCOCTL_HASH \"f8fda77552eb1cdf100d827de38b3f38401237325c541f4e020c94cf75f8cec8\")","+\t\tset(FALCOCTL_HASH \"527a81cba5e42b283466aa74942d0eb6ea044aa969f9cf86f3ef856cbe636b36\")"," \tendif()"," "," \tExternalProject_Add("],"additions":3,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"docker/driver-loader-buster/Dockerfile","lines":["@@ -53,11 +53,19 @@ RUN apt-get update \\"," \tpatchelf \\"," \txz-utils \\"," \tzstd \\","+\t&& if [ \"$TARGETARCH\" = \"amd64\" ]; then apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends libmpx2; fi \\"," \t&& rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*"," ","-RUN if [ \"$TARGETARCH\" = \"amd64\" ]; \\","-\tthen apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends libmpx2; \\","-\tfi","+# The frozen Buster repository cannot supply the eMudhra trust-store fix.","+# Disable the affected anchors, including the legacy AAA cross-signing root,","+# before any HTTPS downloads. Keep the exclusions when regenerating the store.","+RUN sed -i \\","+\t-e 's|^mozilla/emSign_ECC_Root_CA_-_G3.crt$|!&|' \\","+\t-e 's|^mozilla/emSign_Root_CA_-_C1.crt$|!&|' \\","+\t-e 's|^mozilla/emSign_ECC_Root_CA_-_C3.crt$|!&|' \\","+\t-e 's|^mozilla/Comodo_AAA_Services_root.crt$|!&|' \\","+\t/etc/ca-certificates.conf \\","+\t&& update-ca-certificates --fresh"," "," # gcc 6 is no longer included in debian stable, but we need it to"," # build kernel modules on the default debian-based ami used by"],"additions":11,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"docker/driver-loader/Dockerfile","lines":["@@ -42,6 +42,8 @@ RUN apt-get update \\"," \tpatchelf \\"," \txz-utils \\"," \tzstd \\","+\t&& dpkg --compare-versions \"$(dpkg-query -W -f='${Version}' ca-certificates)\" ge '20250419~deb12u2' \\","+\t&& update-ca-certificates --fresh \\"," \t&& rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*"," "," # Some base images have an empty /lib/modules by default"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docker/falco-debian/Dockerfile","lines":["@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@ ENV FALCO_VERSION=\"${FALCO_VERSION}\" \\","     HOME=\"${HOME}\""," "," RUN apt-get -y update && apt-get -y install curl jq ca-certificates gnupg \\","+\t&& dpkg --compare-versions \"$(dpkg-query -W -f='${Version}' ca-certificates)\" ge '20250419~deb12u2' \\","+\t&& update-ca-certificates --fresh \\"," \t&& apt clean -y && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*"," "," WORKDIR /"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docker/falco/Dockerfile","lines":["@@ -24,7 +24,9 @@ ENV FALCO_VERSION=\"${FALCO_VERSION}\" \\","     HOST_ROOT=\"${HOST_ROOT}\" \\","     HOME=\"${HOME}\""," ","-RUN apk update && apk add curl ca-certificates jq libstdc++","+RUN apk add --no-cache --upgrade curl jq libstdc++ openssl \\","+    'ca-certificates>=20260909-r3' 'ca-certificates-bundle>=20260909-r3' \\","+    && update-ca-certificates"," "," WORKDIR /"," "],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/container-trust/README.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@","+# Container CA trust regression test","+","+[check-trust.sh](check-trust.sh) checks the image's OpenSSL trust bundle and hashed CA directory independently. It makes no network requests and changes no trust files. It requires a POSIX shell, OpenSSL, `dirname`, and `grep`.","+","+Run it inside the image, with this directory mounted read-only:","+","+```sh","+docker run --rm --network none --entrypoint /bin/sh \\","+  -v \"$PWD/test/container-trust:/trust:ro\" IMAGE \\","+  -c '/trust/check-trust.sh && update-ca-certificates --fresh && /trust/check-trust.sh'","+```","+","+The second run detects trust restored by certificate-store regeneration. Use a disposable container for regeneration. The script defaults to `/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt` and `/etc/ssl/certs`; optional positional arguments select a different bundle and hashed directory. `OPENSSL` can select an executable. These overrides also allow host-side inspection of extracted stores, but that does not test the image's own OpenSSL or regeneration command.","+","+## Checks","+","+- All 14 [eMudhra advisory](https://emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com/) server chains must fail with OpenSSL trust error 20 in **both** store modes. Certificate expiry, hostname mismatch, malformed fixtures and unsupported command options are failures of the test, not evidence of distrust.","+- Every advisory chain must first **pass** against the explicit historical trust roots in [legacy-roots.pem](fixtures/controls/legacy-roots.pem). This confirms that each fixture still detects the original exposure.","+- A legitimate [download.falco.org chain](fixtures/controls/download.falco.org.pem) must pass server-purpose and hostname verification through each tested store. It must fail against the unrelated legacy roots, checking that implicit system trust cannot rescue an explicit store.","+- The unaffected [ISRG Root X1](fixtures/controls/isrg-root-x1.pem) and [DigiCert Global Root G2](fixtures/controls/digicert-global-root-g2.pem) must remain trusted in both stores. Roots use purpose `any`, because a CA's key usage need not allow it to act as a server leaf.","+","+All verifications use **2026-10-23T12:00:00Z** (`1792756800`), when the saved server chains are valid. The short-lived advisory leaves would otherwise stop detecting regressions after expiry. Do not change this time without revalidating every fixture and control.","+","+The script disables default CA files and directories. It also disables the default CA store on OpenSSL versions that provide that option; OpenSSL 1.1.1 has no separate CA-store option. File checks cannot fall back to the image's directory, and directory checks cannot fall back to its bundle. Positive directory checks require working hash entries, not just PEM files in a directory.","+","+This checks OpenSSL chain validation and trust-store contents. It does not test revocation, Certificate Transparency enforcement, Go's verifier, or a network TLS handshake. A separate live HTTPS smoke test can check the current-time network path.","+","+## Fixture provenance","+","+Only public certificates are included; there are no private keys. **Never install the legacy roots into an image's trust store.** They are deliberately trusted only in isolated test invocations.","+","+| Files | Source |","+|---|---|","+| [rejected/](fixtures/rejected/) — 14 complete server chains, leaf first | The advisory's published offline chain archive, retrieved 2026-10-23. Its README dates the captures to October 20 and the two `noct` chains to October 22. The non-`aaa` chains use the emSign ECC G3 trust path; the `aaa` variants use AAA Certificate Services. The `noct` variants omit SCTs. |","+| [legacy-roots.pem](fixtures/controls/legacy-roots.pem) | AAA Certificate Services and emSign ECC Root CA - G3 public roots, extracted from [certifi 2024.12.14](https://github.com/certifi/python-certifi/blob/2024.12.14/certifi/cacert.pem), which carries the historical Mozilla root collection. |","+| [isrg-root-x1.pem](fixtures/controls/isrg-root-x1.pem), [digicert-global-root-g2.pem](fixtures/controls/digicert-global-root-g2.pem) | Unmodified public root certificates from the same historical certifi collection. |","+| [download.falco.org.pem](fixtures/controls/download.falco.org.pem) | Public chain captured from `download.falco.org:443` with SNI on 2026-10-26: leaf → Let's Encrypt YR2 → cross-signed ISRG Root YR → trusted ISRG Root X1. The fixture contains the three server-supplied certificates, not the self-signed root. The leaf is valid September 25–December 24, 2026. |","+","+[SHA256SUMS](fixtures/SHA256SUMS) records the curated PEM file hashes. To verify them from this directory:","+","+```sh","+(cd fixtures && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS)","+```","+","+When adding or replacing fixtures, verify the positive result against their explicit historical anchors, the rejection against fixed stores, and the independent positive server chain at the fixed time. Keep the expected advisory count synchronized only when intentionally changing coverage."],"additions":45,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/container-trust/check-trust.sh","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@","+#!/bin/sh","+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+# Copyright (C) 2026 The Falco Authors.","+# Offline regression test for the eMudhra CA distrust, using the image's OpenSSL.","+set -eu","+export LC_ALL=C","+","+if [ \"$#\" -gt 2 ]; then","+    echo \"Usage: $0 [CA_BUNDLE [CA_PATH]]\" >&2","+    exit 2","+fi","+","+bundle=${1:-/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt}","+capath=${2:-/etc/ssl/certs}","+openssl=${OPENSSL:-openssl}","+fixtures=$(CDPATH= cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/fixtures\" && pwd)","+# The advisory leaves are deliberately short-lived. Never use the current time.","+verify_time=1792756800 # 2026-10-23T12:00:00Z","+","+fail() {","+    printf 'FAIL: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2","+    exit 1","+}","+","+command -v \"$openssl\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"openssl is required\"","+[ -s \"$bundle\" ] || fail \"missing or empty CA bundle: $bundle\"","+[ -d \"$capath\" ] || fail \"missing CA directory: $capath\"","+set -- \"$fixtures\"/rejected/*.pem","+[ \"$#\" -eq 14 ] || fail \"expected exactly 14 advisory chain fixtures\"","+","+# OpenSSL 1.1.1 has no CAstore option; OpenSSL 3 adds another default store.","+# Disable every implicit source, even when an explicit CAfile/CApath is supplied.","+verify_help=$(\"$openssl\" verify -help 2>&1 || true)","+has_castore=false","+case \"$verify_help\" in *-no-CAstore*) has_castore=true ;; esac","+","+verify() {","+    store_mode=$1","+    store=$2","+    certificate=$3","+    hostname=$4","+    set -- -no-CAfile -no-CApath -attime \"$verify_time\"","+    if [ \"$has_castore\" = true ]; then","+        set -- \"$@\" -no-CAstore","+    fi","+    case \"$store_mode\" in","+        bundle) set -- \"$@\" -CAfile \"$store\" ;;","+        capath) set -- \"$@\" -CApath \"$store\" ;;","+        *) fail \"unknown trust-store mode: $store_mode\" ;;","+    esac","+    if [ -n \"$hostname\" ]; then","+        set -- \"$@\" -purpose sslserver -verify_hostname \"$hostname\"","+    else","+        # A root CA is not itself a server leaf (its key usage may only allow","+        # signing certificates). Check its presence in the store without asking","+        # it to authenticate as a TLS server.","+        set -- \"$@\" -purpose any","+    fi","+    \"$openssl\" verify \"$@\" -untrusted \"$certificate\" \"$certificate\"","+}","+","+expect() {","+    expected=$1","+    label=$2","+    shift 2","+    status=0","+    result=$(verify \"$@\" 2>&1) || status=$?","+    case \"$expected\" in","+        accept)","+            if [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]; then","+                printf '%s\\n' \"$result\" >&2","+                fail \"$label must verify\"","+            fi","+            ;;","+        reject)","+            [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ] || fail \"$label is unexpectedly trusted\"","+            # Require missing trust, not expiry, hostname mismatch, parse errors,","+            # an unsupported option, or a failed executable. Fixture controls","+            # below independently prove each chain is valid at the fixed time.","+            if ! printf '%s\\n' \"$result\" | grep -Eq 'error 20 at [0-9]+ depth lookup'; then","+                printf '%s\\n' \"$result\" >&2","+                fail \"$label failed for a reason other than missing trust\"","+            fi","+            if printf '%s\\n' \"$result\" | grep -E 'error [0-9]+ at' | grep -Evq 'error 20 at'; then","+                printf '%s\\n' \"$result\" >&2","+                fail \"$label also reported a non-trust verification error\"","+            fi","+            ;;","+        *) fail \"unknown expected result: $expected\" ;;","+    esac","+    printf 'PASS: %s (%s)\\n' \"$label\" \"$expected\"","+}","+","+printf 'Checking trust at 2026-10-23T12:00:00Z with %s\\n' \"$(\"$openssl\" version)\"","+","+# Explicit legacy trust proves that all 14 fixtures would expose the regression.","+# These roots are test inputs only; they must never be installed in the image.","+legacy_roots=$fixtures/controls/legacy-roots.pem","+for chain in \"$fixtures\"/rejected/*.pem; do","+    host=${chain##*/}","+    host=${host%.pem}","+    expect accept \"legacy control: $host\" bundle \"$legacy_roots\" \"$chain\" \"$host\"","+done","+","+positive=$fixtures/controls/download.falco.org.pem","+# An unrelated explicit store must not silently fall back to system trust.","+expect reject 'isolated-store control: download.falco.org' bundle \"$legacy_roots\" \"$positive\" download.falco.org","+","+for mode in bundle capath; do","+    case \"$mode\" in bundle) store=$bundle ;; capath) store=$capath ;; esac","+    expect accept \"$mode: download.falco.org\" \"$mode\" \"$store\" \"$positive\" download.falco.org","+    for root in isrg-root-x1 digicert-global-root-g2; do","+        expect accept \"$mode: unaffected $root\" \"$mode\" \"$store\" \"$fixtures/controls/$root.pem\" ''","+    done","+    for chain in \"$fixtures\"/rejected/*.pem; do","+        host=${chain##*/}","+        host=${host%.pem}","+        expect reject \"$mode: $host\" \"$mode\" \"$store\" \"$chain\" \"$host\"","+    done","+done","+","+echo 'PASS: both trust stores reject all 14 compromised chains and preserve the positive controls'"],"additions":122,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/container-trust/fixtures/SHA256SUMS","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@","+5d550643b6400d4341550a9b14aedd0b4fac33ae5deb7d8247b6b4f799c13306  controls/digicert-global-root-g2.pem","+29e79f220ca013f22e95db1ea488742607f7e683efa7b889e98f838463cb63ba  controls/download.falco.org.pem","+22b557a27055b33606b6559f37703928d3e4ad79f110b407d04986e1843543d1  controls/isrg-root-x1.pem","+3cbcc3e794449430c7d15a4d8f26eb3341698a01717b392d99ba702793afb74b  controls/legacy-roots.pem","+3641ff8e872e4c90d5691edb09894914121b267e6a50455347c5f28708fa1af2  rejected/dv-g3b-aaa-emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com.pem","+a360266958b7dfc04250553f6a5f55be769457f126bfd4de415bbaffc9cf62ad  rejected/dv-g3b-aaa-noct-emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com.pem","+ab6483de0cb01d53d59275baf74d2766f3599e57a48d3319e4a5536c268ac696  rejected/dv-g3b-emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com.pem","+de597b4e346d6e84d264a6bc62f5cb5bf4a4d64ec5e587edc446016e4aa693c5  rejected/dv-g3b-noct-emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com.pem","+23641e6de1b0c5a452bd0aaaaa1647863cf5daf27e0b62611ea9289dc0106d39  rejected/dv-g3c-aaa-emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com.pem","+370e97ac882a900d25bda5b8ffe0136197e41d1ab424c3f04adad77825283803  rejected/dv-g3c-emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com.pem","+19fcef2a9fa3ecc88294736d1bdcc2cd7c8753960ff67e8890affa13bd5ea4e5  rejected/ev-g3b-aaa-emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com.pem","+000c2f6b03a9903488ee18e09c6b86e22c2476d0052e11888e5f924de6ad0d44  rejected/ev-g3b-emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com.pem","+6a3019bee019f96570bffca9002637655e7fa8221a370021ca6e0b0fd66f576d  rejected/ev-g3c-aaa-emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com.pem","+636f60b161812118b0474d5fdc1e194aaa1913ebc06331e0f24b324f08b